    {
      "name": "rc_count",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "THE CANONICAL RECOGNITION COUNT (design-audit 6.1, block 354000). Parameterised over the claim NODE: it matches a bare recognizes edge [r -recognizes-> claim] -- binding the SPECIFIC claim -- and sets claim.recognition = Count(InNeighbours(claim, 'recognizes')). Because the count is InNeighbours of the match-bound claim, it is inherently PER-CLAIM (the 6.7 co-load measurement): two recognition families sharing the 'recognizes' edge do NOT cross-contaminate. Fires for ANY recognizes-target -- office authority, ownership claims, tool-ownership -- so bigville_theft/tools compose this instead of re-authoring the count. Idempotent: every match recomputes the same Count, reaching fixpoint.",
      "match": [
        [
          "r",
          "recognizes",
          "claim"
        ]
      ],
      "where": {
        "type": "Lit",
        "value": true
      },
      "effects": [
        [
          "set_attr",
          "claim",
          "recognition",
          {
            "__term__": {
              "type": "Count",
              "source": {
                "type": "InNeighbours",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "claim"
                },
                "edge_type": "recognizes"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
